---
source: crates/agtrace-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help
---
Replay a synthetic multi-agent workspace (a Claude Code lead with a teammate
and a background subagent, plus a Codex root with a child thread) into a temporary
directory at real-time pace, and watch it with the real workspace watcher and TUI.

No agent logs of your own are needed; nothing outside the temporary directory is
read or written.

Usage: agtrace demo [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --speed <SPEED>
          Replay speed: slow (0.5x), normal (1x, real time) or fast (4x)
          
          [default: normal]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>
          Directory for agtrace database and configuration (defaults to system data directory, or AGTRACE_PATH env var)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format for command results
          
          [default: plain]
          [possible values: plain, json]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Logging verbosity level
          
          [default: info]
          [possible values: error, warn, info, debug, trace]

      --project <PROJECT_ROOT>
          Target project directory (defaults to current directory)

      --all-projects
          Operate on all indexed projects instead of current project only

      --all-worktrees
          Include sessions from all git worktrees of the current repository
